        "summary": "Confirmed: DiscoverableProfileView drops avatarURL.",
        "detail": "## Symptom\nSearch results show the user\u2019s avatar correctly, but opening a **non-friend (discoverable)** profile drops the avatar and shows initials only.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed on main)\nIn `Sources/Features/Friends/FriendProfileView.swift`, `DiscoverableProfileView` builds a `Friend` from `DiscoverableUser` but **omits `avatarURL`**:\n\n```swift\nFriend(id: person.id, name: person.name, username: person.username,\n       initials: person.initials, streak: nil)\n```\n\nSearch rows pass `person.avatarURL` into `AvatarView`, which is why search looks correct and the profile detail does not.\n\n## Fix\nPass `avatarURL: person.avatarURL` when constructing the `Friend` in `DiscoverableProfileView`. `Friend`\u2019s initializer accepts `avatarURL` elsewhere. Keep `streak: nil` for private/non-friend profiles.\n\n## Blocker\nPR blocked \u2014 **reconnect GitHub**. Lane 4 file ownership.",
