        "build": "1.0.7 (41)",
        "kind": "feature",
        "quote": "Add goals, both in hours and to-do type goals. For example i want to study math for 3 hours every day, finish a project, and read a book every day. In that scenario, i would want to have a to-do type for a project and a book, and the math to be checked only after 3 hours add up. Also the hourly goal could be daily, weekly, or monthly. For example I want to study 100h this month, and i want to train 3 days a week. Also, the \"goal\" right now is filled based on app usage not the tag, thats saying \"you were productive for 35mins today\", thats okay and should stay an option, but its limiting because its too vague, it doesnt have tgat satisfaction. Also get some memes after i finish the session. Im using the apo that says after i finish more than 5h \"Your session was longer than 95% of people, thats aura.\" Its corny but maybe add it as an option in settings, it brings charachter to the app",
